                        "entry_id": "03620da1-f99a-3fc2-a913-005cb33ce837",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A man who perceives himself as straight and is the aggressive top in a relationship between two men, especially in prison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0c4c22b-cc59-4f6e-b7e5-e3297abe64ef",
                                "sense_id": "53ccc35d-62a9-396f-9dc2-794bd9a28da2",
                                "text": "The jocker's sexual behavior can therefore be viewed as situational homosexuality.\n2012, \"Men Behind Bars: Sexual Exploitation in Prison\" By Wayne S. Wooden"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d39615b-925f-4775-bf01-baeefbe2673b",
                                "sense_id": "53ccc35d-62a9-396f-9dc2-794bd9a28da2",
                                "text": "More common than the reciprocal and mutually constituted homosexual associations between hoboes were the predatory relationships between older hoboes, or “jockers,” and young initiates, or “punks.”\n2010, Citizen Hobo: How a Century of Homelessness Shaped America By Todd DePastino"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d70f502-a61c-4eec-bb93-639bf0843bf0",
                                "sense_id": "53ccc35d-62a9-396f-9dc2-794bd9a28da2",
                                "text": "As the \"masculine\" or \"active\" partner in prison sexual exchanges, jockers maintained a sexual identity as heterosexual\n2008, Criminal Intimacy: Prison and the Uneven History of Modern American Sexuality by Regina P. Kunzler"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
